whisper: Lesson 6: Your own commands
whisper:
whisper: Once a program gets longer, you'll want to give parts of it names. That's what "to ..." is for.
whisper: "given" says what it takes in (with the kind in brackets), and "returning" says what it hands back.
whisper:
whisper: At the bottom there's a test. A command whose name starts with "test" checks things,
whisper: and F7 (Test) runs all of them. Right now the Mistakes tab says it doesn't know "triple". Fair enough.
whisper:
whisper: Your turn: write "triple" so the test passes. It's nearly the same as "double".
whisper: Keep pressing F7 until you get a tick.

to double, given x (a number), returning a number:
  return x times 2
and the universe said i love you

to greet, given who (text):
  scrawl "Hello, ", who, "!"
and the universe said i love you

genesis:
  greet with "Ann"
  scrawl "Double 21 is ", double with 21
and the universe said i love you

to test my commands:
  check double with 4 is 8
  check triple with 4 is 12
and the universe said i love you
